# **Cleaning**

After decontamination, all instruments should be washed thoroughly in warm (not hot) water and detergent. When high-level disinfection is to be carried out, cleaning is the last chance to physically remove bacterial endospores that are not killed by high-level disinfection.

Warm water with detergent is recommended for cleaning because hot water can coagulate protein, making it more difficult to remove. Detergent is needed because water alone will not remove proteins or oils and is preferable to soap, which may leave a residue.

